    "problem_statement": "stop_never condition incorrectly stops retries immediately\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `stop_never` condition is not working as expected. Instead of never stopping retries (allowing infinite retries), it immediately stops on the first attempt.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport tenacity\n\n@tenacity.retry(stop=tenacity.stop_never)\ndef failing_function():\n    print(\"Attempting...\")\n    raise Exception(\"This should keep retrying\")\n\n# This should retry indefinitely, but stops after first attempt\nfailing_function()\n```\n\nExpected behavior: The function should keep retrying indefinitely and print \"Attempting...\" multiple times.\nActual behavior: The function only attempts once and then raises the exception.\n\nThe issue also affects context manager usage:\n\n```python\nfrom tenacity import Retrying, stop_never\n\nfor attempt in Retrying(stop=stop_never):\n    with attempt:\n        print(\"Trying...\")\n        raise Exception(\"Should keep retrying\")\n```\n\nThis should also retry indefinitely but stops after the first attempt."
  },
